## 1. Context Pointer

This state file governs the **PhD empirical chapter** that integrates four pre-existing working documents into one coherent thesis chapter. The chapter sits inside the IIM Indore FPM thesis as the principal empirical contribution. It is methodologically anchored in Institutional Grammar 2.0 (Siddiki, 2012; Frantz, 2021) and fsQCA (Ragin, 2008; Fiss, 2011; Rihoux & Ragin, 2009).

### 1.1 P1 Boundary Note (READ FIRST AT EVERY DECISION POINT)

> **This chapter is NOT P1.** P1 is the post-defence *Regulation & Governance* (R&G) submission of the typology paper currently sitting as `GIQ_V13.docx` (which was desk-rejected at *Government Information Quarterly* on fit grounds, not substance). P1 is a **standalone descriptive-typological paper** with a 49-instrument corpus and a 3×3 archetype matrix.
>
> The thesis chapter, by contrast, is **causal-configurational**. It uses GIQ_V13's typology *as scaffolding*, not as the contribution. The contribution of the chapter is the fsQCA-derived sufficient configurations for legitimate AI governance outcomes across 10 cases. GIQ_V13 sections appear inside the chapter in **compressed** form, not verbatim.
>
> If at any decision point a question arises whether a particular framing belongs to P1 or to this chapter, the test is: **does it answer "what archetypes exist?" (P1) or "what configurations are sufficient for the outcome?" (chapter)**. The first is descriptive; the second is causal.

