## 9. Theoretical Scaffold

| Theory | Role in chapter | Anchor citations |
|---|---|---|
| **Institutional Grammar 2.0** | ADICO syntax for rule-level coding; foundational methodological grammar | Crawford & Ostrom (1995); Siddiki (2012); Frantz & Siddiki (2021) |
| **Configurational Theory / fsQCA** | Set-theoretic method for identifying sufficient causal configurations | Ragin (2008); Rihoux & Ragin (2009); Fiss (2011) |
| **Responsive Regulation** | Enforcement-pyramid baseline against which Type I configurations sit outside | Ayres & Braithwaite (1992); Braithwaite (2017); Lepers (2023) |
| **Stakeholder Theory** | Justification for SR as a causal condition | Freeman (1984); Veale & Zuiderwijk (2021) |
| **Risk-Based Regulation** | Justification for RL as a causal condition | Baldwin, Cave & Lodge (2012); Black (2010) |
| **Policy Instrument Non-Additivity** | Theoretical anchor for the configurational claim that instruments do not aggregate linearly | Capano & Howlett (2020) |
| **Limited Diversity / Necessary Conditions** | Methodological constraint on small-N fsQCA inference | Dul (2016); Schneider & Wagemann (2012) |
| **INUS Logic (conditional on D4)** | Parsing necessary parts within sufficient conditions | Mackie (1965); Baumgartner & Thiem (2017) |

